---
title: Suite Sparse Matrix Jacobian Factorization Benchmarks
author: Jürgen Fuhrmann, Anastasia Dunca
---

This benchmark times a fresh `solve` (symbolic analysis, numeric factorization and
backsolve) with every sparse LU backend on the small matrices of the SuiteSparse Matrix
Collection, fetched through MatrixDepot.jl: every square matrix with at most 100 rows.
Numerically singular matrices (rank below `n`) are listed as skipped and left out, since
they have no solution to time; ParU also segfaults on at least one of them
(`Pajek/GD01_b`), which would end the whole document. Pattern-only and integer matrices
are converted to `Float64`.

```julia
using BenchmarkTools, Random, VectorizationBase, Statistics
using LinearAlgebra, SparseArrays, LinearSolve, Sparspak
# PureUMFPACK backs PureUMFPACKFactorization via LinearSolvePureUMFPACKExt.
# Use `import` (not `using`): PureUMFPACK ≤0.1 exports `solve`, which collides
# with LinearSolve/CommonSolve. PureKLU / SupernodalLU need no extra load.
import PureUMFPACK
import Pardiso
import ParU_jll
import SciMLBase
using Plots
using MatrixDepot

BenchmarkTools.DEFAULT_PARAMETERS.seconds = 0.5

# Why do I need to set this ?
BenchmarkTools.DEFAULT_PARAMETERS.samples = 10

algs = [
    UMFPACKFactorization(),
    KLUFactorization(),
    PureKLUFactorization(),
    PureUMFPACKFactorization(),
    SupernodalLUFactorization(),
    MKLPardisoFactorize(),
    SparspakFactorization(),
    ParUFactorization()
]
algnames = ["UMFPACK", "KLU", "PureKLU", "PureUMFPACK", "SupernodalLU",
    "Pardiso", "Sparspak", "ParU"]
algnames_transpose = reshape(algnames, 1, length(algnames))

cols = [:red, :blue, :green, :magenta, :turquoise, :orange, :purple, :cyan] # one color per alg

# Filter on the (already-local) index metadata rather than downloading everything:
# square matrices (`m == n`) with at most 100 rows. `mdlist` returns the names as a
# flat vector; `listnames` would return a formatted three-column table instead.
allmatrices = mdlist("*/*" & @pred(m == n && n <= 100))
nmatrices = length(allmatrices)

@info "Total number of matrices: $nmatrices"

times = fill(NaN, nmatrices, length(algs))
timed = falses(nmatrices)
percentage_sparsity = fill(NaN, nmatrices)
spaced_out_sparsity = fill(NaN, nmatrices)
matrix_size = fill(NaN, nmatrices)
bandedness_five = fill(NaN, nmatrices)
bandedness_ten = fill(NaN, nmatrices)
bandedness_twenty = fill(NaN, nmatrices)

function compute_bandedness(A, bandwidth)
    n = size(A, 1)
    total_band_positions = 0
    non_zero_in_band = 0
    bandwidth = bandwidth
    for r in 1:n
        for c in 1:n
            if abs(r - c) <= bandwidth
                total_band_positions += 1  # This position belongs to the band
                if A[r, c] != 0
                    non_zero_in_band += 1  # This element is non-zero in the band
                end
            end
        end
    end

    percentage_filled = non_zero_in_band / total_band_positions * 100
    return percentage_filled
end

```

```julia
for z in 1:nmatrices
    currMTX = allmatrices[z]
    try
        rng = MersenneTwister(123)
        A = mdopen(currMTX).A
        # Pattern (Bool) and integer matrices are factorized as Float64, like the rest.
        A = convert(SparseMatrixCSC{Float64, Int}, A)
        n = size(A, 1)

        mtx_copy = copy(A)

        @info "$n × $n"
        n > 100 && error("Skipping too large matrices")
        # A factorization benchmark needs a solvable system; ParU also segfaults on some
        # singular matrices (e.g. Pajek/GD01_b), which would take down the whole document.
        r = rank(Matrix(A))
        if r < n
            println("$(currMTX) skipped: singular (rank $r < $n).")
            continue
        end

        ## COMPUTING SPACED OUT SPARSITY
        rows, cols = size(mtx_copy)
        new_rows = div(rows, 2)
        new_cols = div(cols, 2)
        condensed = zeros(Int, new_rows, new_cols)
        while size(mtx_copy, 1) > 32 || size(mtx_copy, 2) > 32
            rows, cols = size(mtx_copy)
            new_rows = div(rows, 2)
            new_cols = div(cols, 2)
            condensed = sparse(zeros(Int, new_rows, new_cols))

            for r in 1:2:(rows - 1)
                for c in 1:2:(cols - 1)
                    block = mtx_copy[r:min(r + 1, rows), c:min(c + 1, cols)]
                    condensed[div(r - 1, 2) + 1, div(c - 1, 2) + 1] = (length(nonzeros(block)) >=
                                                                       2) ? 1 : 0
                end
            end
            mtx_copy = condensed
        end

        ## COMPUTING FACTORIZATION TIME
        b = rand(rng, n)
        u0 = rand(rng, n)

        # Untimed correctness gate: a timing only counts when the solve returns a
        # non-failure retcode (`Default` is what Pardiso/Sparspak report on success)
        # and a solution whose relative residual beats both an absolute bound and
        # ten times the dense solve's residual — the dense result is the achievable
        # floor, so ill-conditioned matrices don't falsely fail every backend.
        refres = try
            norm(A * (Matrix(A) \ b) - b) / norm(b)
        catch
            0.0
        end

        for j in 1:length(algs)
            try
                sol = solve(LinearProblem(copy(A), copy(b); u0 = copy(u0),
                    alias = LinearAliasSpecifier(alias_A = true, alias_b = true)),
                    algs[j])
                relres = norm(A * sol.u - b) / norm(b)
                if !(SciMLBase.successful_retcode(sol) ||
                     sol.retcode === SciMLBase.ReturnCode.Default) ||
                   !isfinite(relres) || (relres > 1e-6 && relres > 10 * refres)
                    println("$(currMTX): $(algnames[j]) solve rejected (retcode $(sol.retcode), relative residual $relres vs dense $refres) — excluded.")
                    continue
                end
                times[z, j] = @belapsed solve(prob, $(algs[j])).u setup=(prob = LinearProblem(copy($A),
                    copy($b);
                    u0 = copy($u0),
                    alias = LinearAliasSpecifier(alias_A = true, alias_b = true)))
            catch e
                println("$(currMTX): $(algnames[j]) threw $(typeof(e)) — excluded.")
                continue
            end
        end

        bandedness_five[z] = compute_bandedness(A, 5)
        bandedness_ten[z] = compute_bandedness(A, 10)
        bandedness_twenty[z] = compute_bandedness(A, 20)
        percentage_sparsity[z] = length(nonzeros(A)) / n^2
        spaced_out_sparsity[z] = length(nonzeros(mtx_copy)) * percentage_sparsity[z]
        matrix_size[z] = n
        timed[z] = true

        #=
        p = bar(algnames, times[z, :];
            ylabel = "Time/s",
            yscale = :log10,
            title = "Time on $(currMTX)",
            fmt = :png,
            legend = :outertopright)
        display(p)
        =#

        println("successfully factorized $(currMTX) ($(count(!isnan, times[z, :]))/$(length(algs)) backends)")
    catch e
        println("$(currMTX) failed to factorize.")
        println(e)
    end
end

kept = vec(timed)
times = times[kept, :]
percentage_sparsity = percentage_sparsity[kept]
spaced_out_sparsity = spaced_out_sparsity[kept]
spaced_out_sparsity = replace(spaced_out_sparsity, 0 => 1e-10)
bandedness_five = bandedness_five[kept]
bandedness_five = replace(bandedness_five, 0 => 1e-10)
bandedness_ten = bandedness_ten[kept]
bandedness_ten = replace(bandedness_ten, 0 => 1e-10)
bandedness_twenty = bandedness_twenty[kept]
bandedness_twenty = replace(bandedness_twenty, 0 => 1e-10)
matrix_size = matrix_size[kept]

println("$(count(kept)) of $nmatrices matrices are nonsingular and timed.")
println("Solves rejected by the correctness gate (per backend):")
for j in 1:length(algs)
    println("  $(rpad(algnames[j], 14)) $(count(isnan, times[:, j]))")
end
```

In the latest run, 52 of the 88 square matrices are nonsingular and timed. A
solve only contributes a timing when the backend reports a non-failure retcode
and the returned solution's relative residual is under 1e-6 or within an order
of magnitude of the dense solve's residual (the achievable floor on an
ill-conditioned matrix). The counts printed above show which matrix–backend
pairs failed that gate: in the latest run `Sparspak` is rejected on 23 matrices
(the returned `u` is `NaN`), `Pardiso` on 9, and `SupernodalLU` on `HB/steam3`
(retcode `Infeasible`, residual 0.12 against a dense 5e-15), while the other
five backends solve every timed matrix. Rejected solves keep `NaN` timings and
drop out of the figure and every aggregate below.

```julia
meantimes = [mean(filter(!isnan, times[:, j])) for j in 1:length(algs)]
p = bar(algnames, meantimes;
    ylabel = "Time/s",
    yscale = :log10,
    title = "Mean factorization time",
    fmt = :png,
    legend = :outertopright)
```

```julia
p = scatter(percentage_sparsity, times;
    ylabel = "Time/s",
    yscale = :log10,
    xlabel = "Percentage Sparsity",
    xscale = :log10,
    label = algnames_transpose,
    title = "Factorization Time vs Percentage Sparsity",
    fmt = :png,
    legend = :outertopright)
```

